  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "name": "Best Proofing Software Picks for October 2026",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I choose between Superflow, Filestage, and Atarim for my agency's proofing workflow?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Start with your asset mix and client base. Filestage suits marketing teams deep in the Adobe ecosystem managing multi-stakeholder approvals on rich creative files. Atarim fits WordPress retainer shops that want a branded client portal with scope management built in. Superflow is the better fit if your team juggles multiple asset types across clients and needs automated QA that runs on every deploy, every time, without waiting for someone to remember to check."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which proofing tools work for agencies that need to review live websites beyond uploaded files?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow, Pastel, and Atarim all support live website review, but they differ in how much automation they provide. Pastel requires no snippet and suits quick, low-friction feedback collection. Atarim runs AI scans on demand. Superflow runs AI agents automatically on every deploy, posting pinned findings before any human reviews the page."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Pastel or SureFeedback a good fit for agencies with compliance-sensitive clients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the plan. Pastel offers SOC 2 and SAML/SSO only on its Enterprise plan, so the Pro and Team tiers are ruled out for healthcare, legal, or financial clients that require compliance documentation. SureFeedback does not publicly list SOC 2 on any plan. Superflow carries SOC 2 Type II, HIPAA with BAA, a full audit trail, and data residency options for those conversations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When does Frame.io make sense as part of an agency's proofing stack?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Frame.io makes sense when video production is the primary deliverable and your team works inside Adobe Premiere or Final Cut Pro. It covers frame-accurate review and version stacking well. Where it falls short: no live website review, no Lottie file support, and no automated deploy-triggered QA agents, so video-heavy agencies still need a second tool for the rest of client delivery."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Superflow's per-seat pricing compare to Atarim and Filestage subscriptions?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow charges per team seat, so subscription costs grow with internal headcount; guest seats are always free and unlimited. Atarim Pro has a flat base subscription, with additional charges if you need more AI credits, matching the pricing model shown in the comparison table. Filestage starts at $199/month, so compare the subscription cost and plan limits against your team size. For Superflow, also factor in $10 per site a month for each site on Care."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use one proofing tool for both website QA and video review?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, but only a few tools cover both. Superflow and Filestage support websites plus video in a single workspace, while Frame.io covers video but skips live websites entirely, and Atarim covers websites but not video."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the fastest way to get client feedback without making them create an account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Use a proofing tool with magic-link approval instead of a login-gated portal. Superflow, Filestage, Pastel, and SureFeedback all let guest reviewers comment and approve from a link, while Atarim and Frame.io still require client accounts to participate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I pick a self-hosted proofing tool like SureFeedback or a managed service?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Self-hosting makes sense if data ownership and a fixed license cost matter more than feature depth, since SureFeedback caps dashboard sites by plan and skips AI QA automation. A managed service like Superflow fits better once your agency needs automated checks running on every deploy without someone remembering to trigger them."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a QA checklist in the context of proofing software?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A QA checklist is the set of rules a team checks before a site or asset ships, things like broken links, spelling, accessibility, and OG images. Most proofing tools treat this as a manual task someone runs by hand, while Superflow converts the checklist into AI agents that run it automatically on every deploy."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can proofing tools catch bugs before a client sees them?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Only tools with automated, deploy-triggered checks catch issues before a human looks at the page. Superflow is the only tool in this comparison that runs AI agents on every site change, posting findings as pinned comments before a team member or client ever opens the review."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why do client approval cycles drag on even with a proofing tool in place?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Approval cycles stall when feedback lacks context, like a comment that says 'fix this' with no pin, or when reviewers raise subjective, off-topic notes instead of checklist-based findings. Nielsen Norman Group's research on design critiques found unclear feedback guidelines are a leading cause of derailed reviews, which is why pinned, asset-specific comments matter more than freeform chat threads."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When should an agency switch from email and Slack feedback to a dedicated proofing tool?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Switch once feedback starts living in more than one place, screenshots in email, comments in Slack, approvals nowhere documented. That scatter is exactly what PMI's research links to $75 million at risk per $1 billion spent on poor project communication, and a proofing tool keeps the feedback and the approval record attached to the asset itself."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do proofing tools integrate with project management software like Asana or Jira?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most do, but the depth varies widely. Superflow and Filestage offer two-way sync where comments create tasks and sign-offs close them, while SureFeedback's OttoKit connection is a one-way trigger into tools like Asana or ClickUp, and Pastel only exports comments without task sync at all."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Lottie file review supported by most proofing tools?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No, Lottie support is rare. Superflow is the only tool in this comparison that reviews Lottie files alongside websites, video, PDF, and images; Filestage, Pastel, Atarim, Frame.io, and SureFeedback all skip Lottie entirely."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I look for if my agency works with HIPAA-regulated clients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Look for a BAA offering, not just general security certifications like SOC 2. Among the tools compared here, only Superflow lists HIPAA with a BAA, while Pastel, Atarim, Frame.io, Filestage, and SureFeedback either don't mention HIPAA publicly or limit compliance features to their top-tier plans."
      }
    }
  ],
  "url": "https://usesuperflow.ai/blog/proofing-tools-for-agencies",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-26T16:24:01.506Z",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Chaitanya"
  }
}

